updated_at: "2026-08-28T06:38:49.813Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T06:38:49.225Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T06:38:49.225Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Textual and structured refusal candidates share one admissibility predicate; valid global flags cannot override an invalid command option; a regression proves surface --depth and rejected_value verbose when --json is mentioned first; exact coverage and static gates pass
parent: pm-f05lsg
resolution: Unified refusal candidate admissibility and added a textual --json precedence regression.
expected_result: Structured refusal identity always names the actual rejected non-global option.
actual_result: "Textual and structured refusal candidates now share the same global-output-flag filter, preserving --depth and verbose attribution."
